Let $c$ be the smallest real number such that every sequence of graphs $G_n$ on $n$ vertices containing no $K_5$ as a subgraph and having independence number $\alpha(G_n) = o(n)$ can be made bipartite by removing at most $c n^2 + o(n^2)$ edges. What is the value of $c$?

Answer Choices:
A. \frac{1}{18}
B. \frac1{16}
C. \frac1{36}
D. \frac1{20}

